{"1-3":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"jesse-h3448","name":"Jesse","kind":"person","brief":"David's father","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H4910","lemma":"מָשַׁל","tr":"ma·shal","gloss":"to rule","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":81},{"base":"H5002","lemma":"נְאֻם","tr":"ne·um","gloss":"utterance","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":376},{"base":"H5920","lemma":"עַל","tr":"al","gloss":"Most High","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H2158","lemma":"זָמִיר","tr":"za·mir","gloss":"song","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H5273","lemma":"נָעִים","tr":"na·im","gloss":"pleasant","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H9030","lemma":"נִי","tr":"ni","gloss":"me","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":908},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1075},{"base":"H1696","lemma":"דָבַר","tr":"da·var","gloss":"to speak: speak","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1142},{"base":"H4405","lemma":"מִלָּה","tr":"mil·lah","gloss":"speech","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":38},{"base":"H4899","lemma":"מָשִׁיחַ","tr":"ma·shi·ach","gloss":"anointed","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":39}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2PE","chapter":1,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"For no such prophecy was ever brought forth by the will of man, but men spoke from God as they were carried along by the Holy Spirit.","from":2},{"book":"MAT","chapter":22,"verse":43,"verseEnd":43,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Jesus said to them, “How then does David in the Spirit call Him ‘Lord’? For he says:","from":2},{"book":"1SA","chapter":16,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"So Jesse sent for his youngest son and brought him in. He was ruddy, with beautiful eyes and a handsome appearance. And the LORD said, “Rise and anoint him, for he is the one.”","from":1},{"book":"1SA","chapter":16,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"So Samuel took the horn of oil and anointed him in the presence of his brothers, and the Spirit of the LORD rushed upon David from that day forward. Then Samuel set out and went to Ramah.","from":1},{"book":"2SA","chapter":22,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"For who is God besides the LORD? And who is the Rock except our God?","from":3},{"book":"DEU","chapter":32,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"He is the Rock, His work is perfect; all His ways are just. A God of faithfulness without injustice, righteous and upright is He.","from":3},{"book":"2SA","chapter":7,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Now then, you are to tell My servant David that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: I took you from the pasture, from following the flock, to be the ruler over My people Israel.","from":1},{"book":"2SA","chapter":7,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"I have been with you wherever you have gone, and I have cut off all your enemies from before you. Now I will make for you a name like that of the greatest in the land.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"judges-era","title":"Judges era and the road to David","people":2}]},"4-5":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H1242","lemma":"בֹּ֫קֶר","tr":"bo·qer","gloss":"morning","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":214},{"base":"H1877","lemma":"דֶּ֫שֶׁא","tr":"de·she","gloss":"grass","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H2224","lemma":"זָרַח","tr":"za·rach","gloss":"to rise","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"H5051","lemma":"נֹ֫גַהּ","tr":"no·gah","gloss":"brightness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":19},{"base":"H5645","lemma":"עָב","tr":"av","gloss":"cloud","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":31},{"base":"H6779","lemma":"צָמַח","tr":"tsa·mach","gloss":"to spring","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":33},{"base":"H3468","lemma":"יֵ֫שַׁע","tr":"ye·sah","gloss":"salvation","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":36},{"base":"H4306","lemma":"מָטַר","tr":"ma·tar","gloss":"rain","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":38},{"base":"H2656","lemma":"חֵ֫פֶץ","tr":"che·phets","gloss":"pleasure","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":39},{"base":"H6186","lemma":"עָרַךְ","tr":"a·rakh","gloss":"to arrange","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":75}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ISA","chapter":55,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Incline your ear and come to Me; listen, so that your soul may live. I will make with you an everlasting covenant— My loving devotion promised to David.","from":5},{"book":"JDG","chapter":5,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"So may all your enemies perish, O LORD! But may those who love You shine like the sun at its brightest.” And the land had rest for forty years.","from":4},{"book":"2SA","chapter":7,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"I will be his Father, and he will be My son. When he does wrong, I will discipline him with the rod of men and with the blows of the sons of men.","from":5},{"book":"2SA","chapter":7,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Your house and kingdom will endure forever before Me, and your throne will be established forever.”","from":5},{"book":"ISA","chapter":9,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given, and the government will be upon His shoulders. And He will be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace.","from":5},{"book":"ISA","chapter":9,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Of the increase of His government and peace there will be no end. He will reign on the throne of David and over his kingdom, to establish and sustain it with justice and righteousness from that time and forevermore. The zeal of the LORD of Hosts will accomplish this.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":89,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I will forever preserve My loving devotion for him, and My covenant with him will stand fast.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":89,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"I will establish his line forever, his throne as long as the heavens endure.","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"6-7":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H8313","lemma":"שָׂרַף","tr":"sa·raph","gloss":"to burn","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":117},{"base":"H7675","lemma":"שֶׁ֫בֶת","tr":"she·vet","gloss":"seat","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H6975","lemma":"קוֹץ","tr":"qots","gloss":"thorn","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H1100","lemma":"בְּלִיַּ֫עַל","tr":"be·liy·ya·al","gloss":"Belial","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":27},{"base":"H5074","lemma":"נָדַד","tr":"na·dad","gloss":"to wander","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":28},{"base":"H2595","lemma":"חֲנִית","tr":"cha·nit","gloss":"spear","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":47},{"base":"H1270","lemma":"בַּרְזֶל","tr":"bar·zel","gloss":"iron","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":76},{"base":"H5060","lemma":"נָגַע","tr":"na·ga","gloss":"to touch","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":150},{"base":"H4390","lemma":"מָלֵא","tr":"ma·le","gloss":"to fill","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":249},{"base":"H6086","lemma":"עֵץ","tr":"ets","gloss":"tree: wood","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":330}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":3,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Both thorns and thistles it will yield for you, and you will eat the plants of the field.","from":6},{"book":"DEU","chapter":13,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"that wicked men have arisen from among you and have led the people of their city astray, saying, “Let us go and serve other gods” (which you have not known),","from":6},{"book":"1SA","chapter":2,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now the sons of Eli were wicked men; they had no regard for the LORD","from":6},{"book":"2SA","chapter":20,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now a worthless man named Sheba son of Bichri, a Benjamite, happened to be there, and he blew the ramʼs horn and shouted: “We have no share in David, no inheritance in Jesseʼs son. Every man to his tent, O Israel!”","from":6},{"book":"2SA","chapter":22,"verse":8,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the earth shook and quaked; the foundations of the heavens trembled; they were shaken because He burned with anger. Smoke rose from His nostrils, and consuming fire came from His mouth; glowing coals blazed forth. He parted the heavens and came down with dark clouds beneath His feet.","from":7},{"book":"SNG","chapter":2,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Like a lily among the thorns is my darling among the maidens.","from":6},{"book":"ISA","chapter":27,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"I am not angry. If only thorns and briers confronted Me, I would march and trample them, I would burn them to the ground.","from":7},{"book":"ISA","chapter":33,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The peoples will be burned to ashes, like thorns cut down and set ablaze.","from":6}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"8-12":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"adino-h5722","name":"Adino","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"eznites-h6112g","name":"Eznites","kind":"person","brief":"Adino's clan","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"hachmonites-h2453g","name":"Hachmonites","kind":"person","brief":"Family of warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"jashobeam-h3434g","name":"Jashobeam","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"ahoah-h0265","name":"Ahoah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"dodo-h1734h","name":"Dodo","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"eleazar-h0499i","name":"Eleazar","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"agee-h0089","name":"Agee","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Shammah","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"hararites-h2043","name":"Hararites","kind":"person","brief":"Family of warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"shammah-h8037g","name":"Shammah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"places":[{"id":"philistia-h6429","name":"Philistia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"lehi-h3896","name":"Lehi","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"words":[{"base":"H6430","lemma":"פְּלִשְׁתִּי","tr":"pe·lish·ti","gloss":"Philistine","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":288},{"base":"H3429","lemma":"יֹשֵׁב בַּשֶּׁ֫בֶת","tr":"yo·shev bash·she·vet","gloss":"Josheb-basshebeth","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H2513","lemma":"חֶלְקָה","tr":"chel·qah","gloss":"portion","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":29},{"base":"H8668","lemma":"תְּשׁוּעָה","tr":"te·shu·ah","gloss":"deliverance: salvation","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":34},{"base":"H0310","lemma":"אַחַר","tr":"a·char","gloss":"after","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":715},{"base":"H1368","lemma":"גִּבּוֹר","tr":"gib·bor","gloss":"mighty man","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":159},{"base":"H0622","lemma":"אָסַף","tr":"a·saph","gloss":"to gather","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":200},{"base":"H8037","lemma":"שַׁמָּא","tr":"sham·ma","gloss":"Shammah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H5742","lemma":"עֲדָשָׁה","tr":"a·dash","gloss":"lentil","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","tr":"na·khah","gloss":"to smite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":500}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CH","chapter":11,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Next in command was Eleazar son of Dodo the Ahohite, one of the three mighty men.","from":9},{"book":"1CH","chapter":11,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"But Eleazar and David stationed themselves in the middle of the field and defended it. They struck down the Philistines, and the LORD brought about a great victory.","from":9},{"book":"1CH","chapter":27,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Dodai the Ahohite was in charge of the division for the second month, and Mikloth was the leader. There were 24,000 men in his division.","from":9},{"book":"NUM","chapter":23,"verse":7,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Balaam lifted up an oracle, saying: “Balak brought me from Aram, the king of Moab from the mountains of the east. ‘Come,’ he said, ‘put a curse on Jacob for me; come and denounce Israel!’ How can I curse those whom God has not cursed? How can I denounce those whom the LORD has not denounced?","from":9},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the LORD threw them into confusion before Israel, who defeated them in a great slaughter at Gibeon, pursued them along the ascent to Beth-horon, and struck them down as far as Azekah and Makkedah.","from":10},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And because the LORD, the God of Israel, fought for Israel, Joshua captured all these kings and their land in one campaign.","from":10},{"book":"JOS","chapter":11,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and the LORD delivered them into the hand of Israel, who struck them down and pursued them all the way to Greater Sidon and Misrephoth-maim, and eastward as far as the Valley of Mizpeh. They struck them down, leaving no survivors.","from":10},{"book":"JDG","chapter":15,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Samson arrived in Lehi, the Philistines came out shouting against him. And the Spirit of the LORD came mightily upon him. The ropes on his arms became like burnt flax, and the bonds broke loose from his hands.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"13-17":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":4,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"philistia-h6429","name":"Philistia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"adullam-h5725","name":"Adullam","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"rephaim-valley-h7497g","name":"Rephaim Valley","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"bethlehem-h1035g","name":"Bethlehem","kind":"place","brief":"In Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":14}],"words":[{"base":"H1035","lemma":"בֵּית לֶ֫חֶם","tr":"bet le·chem","gloss":"Bethlehem","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":82},{"base":"H0877","lemma":"בֹּאר","tr":"bor","gloss":"cistern","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1075},{"base":"H6430","lemma":"פְּלִשְׁתִּי","tr":"pe·lish·ti","gloss":"Philistine","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":288},{"base":"H7969","lemma":"שָׁלֹשׁ","tr":"sha·losh","gloss":"three","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":431},{"base":"H0014","lemma":"אָבָה","tr":"a·vah","gloss":"be willing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":54},{"base":"H0227","lemma":"אָז","tr":"az","gloss":"then","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":141},{"base":"H1368","lemma":"גִּבּוֹר","tr":"gib·bor","gloss":"mighty man","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":159},{"base":"H8354","lemma":"שָׁתָה","tr":"sha·tah","gloss":"to drink","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":217},{"base":"H8179","lemma":"שַׁ֫עַר","tr":"sha·ar","gloss":"gate","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":374}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":22,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So David left Gath and took refuge in the cave of Adullam. When his brothers and the rest of his fatherʼs household heard about it, they went down to him there.","from":13},{"book":"1SA","chapter":22,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"So he left them in the care of the king of Moab, and they stayed with him the whole time David was in the stronghold.","from":14},{"book":"1SA","chapter":22,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Then the prophet Gad said to David, “Do not stay in the stronghold. Depart and go into the land of Judah.” So David left and went to the forest of Hereth.","from":14},{"book":"2SA","chapter":5,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Now the Philistines had come and spread out in the Valley of Rephaim.","from":13},{"book":"GEN","chapter":35,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"So Jacob set up a pillar in the place where God had spoken with him—a stone marker—and he poured out a drink offering on it and anointed it with oil.","from":16},{"book":"LEV","chapter":17,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"If anyone from the house of Israel or a foreigner living among them eats any blood, I will set My face against that person and cut him off from among his people.","from":17},{"book":"JHN","chapter":4,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But whoever drinks the water I give him will never thirst. Indeed, the water I give him will become in him a fount of water springing up to eternal life.”","from":15},{"book":"2CO","chapter":5,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"For Christʼs love compels us, because we are convinced that One died for all, therefore all died.","from":16}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"18-23":{"people":[{"id":"abishai-h0052","name":"Abishai","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"joab-h3097g","name":"Joab","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"zeruiah-h6870g","name":"Zeruiah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of David","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"benaiah-h1141g","name":"Benaiah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":2,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"jehoiada-h3077g","name":"Jehoiada","kind":"person","brief":"Father of warrior Benaiah","count":2,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"ariel-h0739","name":"Ariel","kind":"person","brief":"A Moabite","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":23}],"places":[{"id":"kabzeel-h6909","name":"Kabzeel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"words":[{"base":"H7969","lemma":"שָׁלֹשׁ","tr":"sha·losh","gloss":"three","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":431},{"base":"H2595","lemma":"חֲנִית","tr":"cha·nit","gloss":"spear","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":47},{"base":"H4713","lemma":"מִצְרִי","tr":"mits·ri","gloss":"Egyptian","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":70},{"base":"H1141","lemma":"בְּנָיָ֫הוּ","tr":"be·na·yah","gloss":"Benaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":42},{"base":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","tr":"na·khah","gloss":"to smite","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":500},{"base":"H3077","lemma":"יְהוֹיָדָע","tr":"ye·ho·ya·da","gloss":"Jehoiada","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":51},{"base":"H3513","lemma":"כָּבֵד","tr":"ka·vad","gloss":"to honor: honour","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":113},{"base":"H0739","lemma":"אֲרִיאֵל","tr":"a·ri·el","gloss":"Ariel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3381","lemma":"יָרַד","tr":"ya·rad","gloss":"to go down","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":380},{"base":"H6909","lemma":"קַבְצְאֵל","tr":"qav·tse·el","gloss":"Kabzeel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":15,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the chiefs of Edom will be dismayed; trembling will seize the leaders of Moab; those who dwell in Canaan will melt away,","from":20},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"These were the southernmost cities of the tribe of Judah in the Negev toward the border of Edom: Kabzeel, Eder, Jagur,","from":20},{"book":"JDG","chapter":14,"verse":5,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Samson went down to Timnah with his father and mother and came to the vineyards of Timnah. Suddenly a young lion came roaring at him, and the Spirit of the LORD came powerfully upon him, and he tore the lion apart with his bare hands as one would tear a young goat. But he did not tell his father or mother what he had done.","from":20},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":34,"verseEnd":37,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"David replied, “Your servant has been tending his fatherʼs sheep, and whenever a lion or a bear came and carried off a lamb from the flock, I went after it, struck it down, and delivered the lamb from its mouth. If it reared up against me, I would grab it by its fur, strike it down, and kill it. Your servant has killed lions and bears; this uncircumcised Philistine will be like one of them, for he has defied the armies of the living God.” David added, “The LORD, who delivered me from the claws of the lion and the bear, will deliver me from the hand of this Philistine.” “Go,” said Saul, “and may the LORD be with you.”","from":20},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":51,"verseEnd":51,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"David ran and stood over him. He grabbed the Philistineʼs sword and pulled it from its sheath and killed him; and he cut off his head with the sword. When the Philistines saw that their hero was dead, they turned and ran.","from":21},{"book":"1SA","chapter":22,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Ahimelech answered the king, “Who among all your servants is as faithful as David, the kingʼs son-in-law, the captain of your bodyguard and honored in your house?","from":23},{"book":"1SA","chapter":26,"verse":6,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And David asked Ahimelech the Hittite and Abishai son of Zeruiah, Joabʼs brother, “Who will go down with me to Saul in the camp?” “I will go with you,” answered Abishai. That night David and Abishai came to the troops, and Saul was lying there asleep in the inner circle of the camp, with his spear stuck in the ground by his head. And Abner and the troops were lying around him. Abishai said to David, “Today God has delivered your enemy into your hand. Now, therefore, please let me thrust the spear through him into the ground with one stroke. I will not need to strike him twice!”","from":18},{"book":"2SA","chapter":1,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Saul and Jonathan, beloved and delightful in life, were not divided in death. They were swifter than eagles; they were stronger than lions.","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":4}]},"24-39":{"people":[{"id":"joab-h3097g","name":"Joab","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":2,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"asahel-h6214g","name":"Asahel","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"dodo-h1734i","name":"Dodo","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"elhanan-h0445h","name":"Elhanan","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"elika-h0470","name":"Elika","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"shammah-h8048h","name":"Shammah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"helez-h2503g","name":"Helez","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"ikkesh-h6142","name":"Ikkesh","kind":"person","brief":"Father of warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":26}