","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"ammon-h5983","name":"Ammon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":37},{"id":"beeroth-h0881g","name":"Beeroth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":37}],"words":[{"base":"H0045","lemma":"אֲבִי־עַלְבוֹן","tr":"a·vi-al·von","gloss":"Abi-albon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H2733","lemma":"חֲרֹדִי","tr":"cha·ro·di","gloss":"Harodite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H2043","lemma":"הֲרָרִי","tr":"ha·ra·ri","gloss":"Hararite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H3505","lemma":"יִתְרִי","tr":"yit·ri","gloss":"Ithrite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H5896","lemma":"עִירָא","tr":"i·ra","gloss":"Ira","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H8048","lemma":"שַׁמָּה","tr":"sham·mah","gloss":"Shammah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"H5200","lemma":"נְטֹפָתִי","tr":"ne·to·pha·ti","gloss":"Netophathite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H6214","lemma":"עֲשָׂהאֵל","tr":"a·sa·h·el","gloss":"Asahel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":24},{"base":"H1035","lemma":"בֵּית לֶ֫חֶם","tr":"bet le·chem","gloss":"Bethlehem","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":82},{"base":"H3097","lemma":"יוֹאָב","tr":"yo·av","gloss":"Joab","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":145}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":2,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The three sons of Zeruiah were there: Joab, Abishai, and Asahel. Now Asahel was fleet of foot like a wild gazelle,","from":24},{"book":"2SA","chapter":11,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So David sent and inquired about the woman, and he was told, “This is Bathsheba, the daughter of Eliam and the wife of Uriah the Hittite.”","from":34},{"book":"2SA","chapter":11,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So David sent and inquired about the woman, and he was told, “This is Bathsheba, the daughter of Eliam and the wife of Uriah the Hittite.”","from":39},{"book":"1CH","chapter":2,"verse":53,"verseEnd":53,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and the clans of Kiriath-jearim—the Ithrites, Puthites, Shumathites, and Mishraites. From these descended the Zorathites and Eshtaolites.","from":38},{"book":"DEU","chapter":1,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They left and went up into the hill country, and came to the Valley of Eshcol and spied out the land.","from":30},{"book":"JDG","chapter":2,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They buried him in the land of his inheritance, at Timnath-heres in the hill country of Ephraim, north of Mount Gaash.","from":30},{"book":"JDG","chapter":12,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Abdon son of Hillel, from Pirathon, died, and he was buried at Pirathon in Ephraim, in the hill country of the Amalekites.","from":30},{"book":"2SA","chapter":11,"verse":6,"verseEnd":27,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"At this, David sent orders to Joab: “Send me Uriah the Hittite.” So Joab sent him to David. When Uriah came to him, David asked how Joab and the troops were doing and how the war was going. Then he said to Uriah, “Go down to your house and wash your feet.” So Uriah left the palace, and a gift from the king followed him. But Uriah slept at the door of the palace with all his masterʼs servants; he did not go down to his house. And David was told, “Uriah did not go home.” “Havenʼt you just arrived from a journey?” David asked Uriah. “Why didnʼt you go home?”","from":39}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":4}]}}